# Deliverables — Markdown in the repo

Reports, docs and diagrams are delivered as plain `.md` files committed into the
relevant repo.

- **Never** publish via a cloud artifact tool (e.g. claude.ai Artifacts).
- **Never** generate a styled `.html` report — no self-contained pages with
  embedded CSS, no light/dark theme blocks, no "same design an Artifact would
  have used".
- If a Markdown file and an HTML twin would say the same thing, write only the
  Markdown one.
- Diagrams go in fenced code blocks as ASCII, or Mermaid where the host renders it.

Why: the HTML twins are unreadable in review, unreadable in a diff, and duplicate
content that already lives in the `.md`. One file, one source of truth.

Hub push exception still applies: in `new-project-idea` and `opencode-24-7-hub`,
commit locally only — don't `git push` unless the owner asks in that session.
